{
 "study": "THE ENTANGLEMENT (v1.40)",
 "question": "Does making old body parts harder to shed let a world keep a complex animal once it has made one?",
 "lever": "Generative entrenchment (Wimsatt). Each part carries la (generations the structural slot has been inherited) and oa (generations since its organ values were last jolted). The shed rate decays with the mean la of the sheddable leaves; eye and mouth drift is damped symmetrically by oa. plast(age)=1/(1+ENTRENCH*age/ENTRENCH_HALF).",
 "gameVersion": "v1.40",
 "baselineVersion": "v1.39.2",
 "runDate": "2026-09-11",
 "design": {
  "paired": "Same eight seeds run twice, lever off and lever on, so seed quality is controlled exactly.",
  "seedsDeclaredBeforeAnyResult": [
   60606,
   1001,
   1002,
   1003,
   1004,
   1005,
   1006,
   1007
  ],
  "arms": {
   "off": "ENTRENCH=0",
   "on": "ENTRENCH=1, ENTRENCH_HALF=20"
  },
  "minutesPerRun": 90,
  "stepsPerRun": 324000,
  "sampleIntervalSteps": 21600,
  "bootstrap": "viewport 1280x720 (R===334 verified), paused=true, versusSeeds/heirSeeds/dynasty/parentDish reset before every initWorld, scenario classic, foodRate 1 and mutRate 0.1 (shipped dial defaults), sterile.",
  "prewrittenSuccessCriterion": "The lever wins only if complete animals (depth>=2, eyed>=25% of population, paddlers present) are standing at the final sample in at least half of the eight seeds."
 },
 "determinism": {
  "instrumentationIsInert": "la/oa add no rnd() draws. Seed 60606 at 18000 steps: fingerprint 2830395165, pop 33, births 312, deaths 349, maxGen 9 on plain v1.38, instrumented v1.38, and instrumented v1.39.2 alike.",
  "leverIsReversible": "With ENTRENCH=0 the same fingerprint 2830395165 is reproduced by the v1.40 build, so the dial returns the dish bit for bit to v1.39.2.",
  "crossMachineWarning": "This machine could NOT reproduce the archived v1.38 crown run for seed 60606. World init matches exactly (same callsign SOUP-C57V-HM, same 70 founders) but the trajectory diverges: at 18000 steps this machine gives pop 33 / births 312 / maxGen 9 where studies/crown-and-replication.json records pop 44 / births 332 / maxGen 10. Local repeats are bit identical, so the divergence is between machines, not between runs. This is the first direct evidence for the untested risk named in PAPER.md section 4, and it matters because the boards' anti cheat design assumes an entry can be re run from its seed and verified."
 },
 "verdict": {
  "result": "FAILED the prewritten criterion",
  "completeAnimalsAtMin90": {
   "off": "1 of 8",
   "on": "1 of 8",
   "required": "4 of 8"
  },
  "oneLine": "Entrenchment does what it claims and it is not enough: parts are held about twice as long and structural depth survives in seven seeds of eight instead of four, but complete animals are no more common, because the binding constraint was never structural retention. It is organ acquisition."
 },
